    <article>
      <h1>Why I'm posting my notes</h1>
      
      <p>
        Hi, I'm Els, a filmmaker with a plan for a personal documentary, a not-commissioned work of art. 
        Independent movie. To explore options, inspiration for making my own film, I started watching other 
        documentaries and taking notes on what I saw. I felt the need to discuss my notes, so that's when 
        I decided to publish them. At first I published these notes on Substack, but for various reasons I 
        decided to move them to my own blog site: this one. I hope that my notes will spark some reactions, 
        I'd really enjoy to meet people to discuss these films with.
      </p>

      <p>
        Posting only texts made the site look utterly dull, I needed a visual for each film. And then it 
        clicked: I should draw my own! So I just started doing that. No screen grabs, but some key element 
        as my interpretation of the film. Unexpected: drawing sparks my imagination and I think it is a 
        very relaxing and fulfilling way to spend time drawing my own visuals.
      </p>

      <p>
        I like making simple websites, and with some help from AI that also became a lot easier. So, that's 
        what I did: make this website and put the notes on it. Hope you enjoy! 
      </p>
    </article>
